\title{A Half-Open Subspace}
\taxon{Example}
\p{
    Give #{A=[0,1]} the [subspace topology](def-000D) inherited from the real
    line. Then
    the subset
    ##{
        \{x\in A\mid 0\leq x<1\}=A\cap(-1,1)
    }
    is open in #{A}, although it is not open in #{\mathbb{R}}. Likewise,
    #{\{x\in A\mid 0<x\leq1\}} is open in #{A}. The word \em{open} therefore
    always refers to an ambient topological space.
}
